# Per-environment app hosts for server-built links (sync-do plan §18.9).
#
# SECOND COPY ON PURPOSE. firebase.json declares two functions codebases —
# `default` (apps/functions) and `study` (apps/study-functions) — and the
# Firebase CLI loads `.env` / `.env.<projectId>` from EACH codebase's own
# `source` directory. Configuring only apps/functions leaves this codebase on
# the production fallbacks, and 14 modules here build email CTAs from
# STUDY_APP_URL. That is the "staging mails testers into production" failure
# arriving through the runbook rather than through the code.
#
# Production sets nothing: the fallbacks in
# packages/shared-functions/src/config/email.ts ARE the production hosts.
#
# Copy to `.env.<your-project-id>` — e.g. `.env.sync-sit-staging`:
SIT_APP_URL=https://<sit-host-for-this-environment>
STUDY_APP_URL=https://<study-host-for-this-environment>
DO_APP_URL=https://<do-host-for-this-environment>
